course: dictionary
lesson: 4964
title: Words about rubbish and science
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An incinerator is a furnace or machine that burns rubbish at very high temperatures until it turns to ash. When you meet a new word, read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «It can be buried in a landfill, burned in an incinerator that often makes electricity from the heat, or sorted and recycled into new materials.»
explain: Look at the other choices in that sentence: buried in a landfill, and sorted and recycled. All three are ways to deal with rubbish, so an incinerator must be another way to get rid of it. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word and check it still makes sense.
explain: Try it: «It can be burned in a furnace or machine that burns rubbish until it turns to ash» makes sense, so the meaning is right. Some incinerators make electricity from the heat, which is a useful clue, but the sentence also reminds you that they are not the only choice.
explain: The phrases «waste incinerator» and «hospital incinerator» show you where the word is used. Waste means rubbish, and a hospital incinerator burns rubbish from a hospital. When context is not enough, a dictionary settles it.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Incinerator» means a furnace or machine for burning rubbish at very high temperatures.
fact: «Incinerator» is a noun. You can have one incinerator or many incinerators.
fact: Some incinerators make electricity from the heat, but they can pollute the air.
fact: «Waste incinerator» and «hospital incinerator» are phrases you may meet in science and geography lessons.
exercise: «It can be buried in a landfill, burned in an incinerator that often makes electricity from the heat, or sorted and recycled into new materials.» What is an incinerator? | *A furnace or machine for burning rubbish until it turns to ash | A machine that sorts rubbish into new materials | A place where rubbish is buried under the ground | A park where children play
exercise: In the same sentence, find and copy one word that means turned into new materials. | *recycled | buried | landfill | incinerator
exercise: In the phrase «waste incinerator», what does waste mean? | *Rubbish or unwanted material | A large, empty field | Wasting time on a game | A kind of cold wind
test: Some incinerators make electricity from the heat. What can the heat from an incinerator be used for, according to the sentence? | Building new houses | *Making electricity | Growing crops in a field | Cooling down the rubbish
test: Which is a problem with incinerators, according to the lessons? | They turn rubbish into water | They make the air cleaner | *They can pollute the air | Their fuel is always free
exam: Using the context and the meaning, what is a hospital incinerator? | *A furnace that burns hospital rubbish until it turns to ash | A room where doctors sleep | A hospital bed on wheels | A place where new medicines are made
